.TH CHARTS 1 "2026-09-17" "charts 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
charts \- ANSI charts for the Linux console
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B charts
.RI [ FILE | \- ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B charts
.IR a.csv " " b.json " " c.tsv " " \-\-tile " " \-t " " bar,line,pie3d
.br
.B charts
.B \-i
.IR dir | file ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B charts
reads CSV, TSV or JSON and draws a chart that fits the screen.
It uses the 16 ANSI console colours with block shading, extruded bars and
ellipsoid pies, double-line frames and drop shadows.
There are no dependencies, no configuration and no runtime: one binary, one
screenful of output.
.PP
Text columns become category labels; numeric columns become series.
Directories expand to the data files inside them.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Output
.TP
.BI \-t,\ \-\-type " NAME"
Chart type. A comma-separated list with
.B \-\-tile
draws several charts at once.
Types:
.BR bar ", " stacked ", " hbar ", " line ", " area ", " pie ", " pie3d ", " donut ", " scatter ", " hist ", " table .
Default
.BR bar .
.TP
.BI \-T,\ \-\-title " TEXT"
Title, drawn into the top border.
.TP
.BI \-\-subtitle " TEXT"
Second centred line under the title.
.TP
.BI \-\-xlabel " TEXT"
Label under the x axis.
.TP
.BI \-\-ylabel " TEXT"
Label up the left side, one character per row.
.TP
.BI \-p,\ \-\-palette " NAME"
Colour set:
.BR dos " (default), " ega ", " cga ", " ice ", " fire ", " green ", " amber ", " mono .
.TP
.BI \-w,\ \-\-width " N"
Force the width in cells. Defaults to the terminal width.
.TP
.BI \-H,\ \-\-height " N"
Force the height in rows.
.TP
.BI \-\-frame " STYLE"
.BR double " (default), " single ", " heavy ", " ascii " or " none .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-shadow
No drop shadow behind the frame.
.TP
.B \-\-tile
Lay several charts out on one screen in a grid.
.TP
.BR \-\-legend ", " \-\-no\-legend
Series legend on or off.
.TP
.BR \-\-values ", " \-\-no\-values
Numbers drawn on the bars.
.TP
.BR \-\-grid ", " \-\-no\-grid
Horizontal grid lines.
.TP
.BR \-\-color ", " \-\-no\-color
Force colour on or off. Colour is dropped when stdout is not a terminal.
.B NO_COLOR
is honoured.
.TP
.B \-\-ascii
ASCII glyphs only, no box drawing or block characters.
.TP
.BI \-o,\ \-\-out " FILE"
Write to FILE instead of stdout.
.SS Data
.TP
.B \-\-xy
The first numeric column is the X axis.
.TP
.B \-\-transpose
Swap rows and columns before anything else.
.TP
.BI \-\-delim " C"
Force the delimiter. Accepts
.BR tab ", " comma ", " semi ", " pipe
or a single character.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-header
Treat the first row as data.
.TP
.BI \-\-labels\-col " N"
Use column N (1-based) for labels.
.TP
.BI \-\-series\-col " N"
Keep only numeric column N as a series.
.TP
.BI \-\-label\-key " K"
JSON: the record field that supplies labels.
.TP
.BI \-\-min " V"
.TP
.BI \-\-max " V"
Pin the value axis.
.TP
.BI \-\-explode " [N]"
Pop slice N out of the pie. Bare
.B \-\-explode
pops the biggest slice.
.TP
.BI \-\-depth " N"
Rows of 3-D extrusion. Default 2, maximum 6.
.TP
.BI \-\-bins " N"
Histogram buckets. Default 10.
.TP
.BI \-\-prec " N"
Fixed number of decimals in value labels.
.SS Running
.TP
.BR \-i,\ \-\-interactive
Full-screen interactive mode. Keys:
.BR c / C
or the arrows change chart type,
.B 1\-9
jump to a type,
.B p / P
change palette,
.B t
shows the table,
.B e
pops a pie slice,
.B v
value labels,
.B g
grid,
.B d / D
deeper or flatter 3-D,
.B n / N
next or previous file,
.B r
reload,
.B w
toggles auto-reload,
.B ?
shows the keys and
.B q
quits.
.TP
.B \-\-watch
Redraw whenever a source file changes. Needs a terminal.
.TP
.B \-\-watch\-ms " N"
Poll interval for
.BR \-\-watch .
.TP
.B \-\-describe
Print what was parsed out of the file, then exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-example " [csv|json]"
Print a sample input file.
.TP
.BR \-\-list\-types ", " \-\-list\-palettes ", " \-\-version ", " \-h
Informational output.
.SH INPUT
.SS CSV and TSV
The delimiter is sniffed from the first non-blank line among
.BR , " " ; ", TAB and " | .
If the first row contains any text it is a header; if every cell is a number the
file has no header and columns are named
.BR col1 ,
.BR col2 ,
etc.
A non-numeric first column becomes the labels, every other numeric column
becomes a series.
Blank lines are skipped and a line beginning with
.B #
is a comment.
Quoted fields may contain the delimiter; a doubled quote inside a quoted field
is one quote.
Numbers may carry thousands separators or a trailing percent sign; a field that
does not parse becomes a gap in that series.
.SS JSON
Accepted shapes:
.IP \(bu 2
an array of records, labels taken from a text field named
.BR label ", " name ", " key ", " category ", " date ", " time ", " month " or " year ;
.IP \(bu 2
an object with
.B labels
and
.BR series ,
each series carrying
.B name
and
.B values ;
.IP \(bu 2
an object of numbers, one series with the keys as labels;
.IP \(bu 2
a flat array of numbers;
.IP \(bu 2
an array of arrays with a text first row;
.IP \(bu 2
an object with parallel
.B x
and
.B y
arrays.
.PP
.B null
and missing fields become gaps.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The chart was drawn.
.TP
.B 1
Bad data, bad option or unreadable file. One line on stderr beginning
.BR "charts: " .
.TP
.B 2
No input, or
.B \-i
or
.B \-\-watch
without a terminal.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set and non-empty, colour is off.
.TP
.BR COLUMNS ", " LINES
Used for the chart size when the terminal size cannot be read.
.TP
.B TERM
Not consulted for capability; the classic 16 SGR colours are used always.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B charts revenue.csv -t pie3d -T 'Revenue mix'
An extruded pie with the file named in the frame.
.TP
.B charts quarterly.csv -t stacked --values --ylabel units
Stacked bars with the totals printed on top.
.TP
.B charts disk.json -t hbar --palette ice
Horizontal bars in a cool palette.
.TP
.B charts a.csv b.csv c.csv d.csv --tile -t bar,line,pie3d,stacked
Four charts, one screen, four types.
.TP
.B charts -i examples/
Browse a directory of data interactively.
.TP
.B cat data.csv | charts -t bar
From a pipe.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gnuplot (1),
.BR asciigraph (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written for the Linux console by John Stamagal.
